### Get Entra ID token

# Retrieves a service-to-service OAuth2 token from Microsoft Entra ID using the client credentials flow.
# The token can then be used as a Bearer token in requests to protected DAL endpoints.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   - Set entraClientId and entraClientSecret under `test` env in http-client.private.env.json (never commit this file)
#   - Select the `test` environment in your HTTP client
#
# Usage:
#   1. Run this request first to obtain a token
#   2. Reference the token when using the DAL GraphQL explorer using headers:
#      `Authorization: Bearer {{getEntraToken.response.body.access_token}}`
#      email: testuser11 at defra.gov.uk

# @name getEntraToken

POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/6f504113-6b64-43f2-ade9-242e05780007/oauth2/v2.0/token HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&
client_id={{entraClientId}}&
client_secret={{entraClientSecret}}&
scope={{entraClientId}}/.default
